# Portainer endpoints

## Gate

Use when the user authorized Portainer work and the turn needs **endpoint**
(environment) inventory: list environments, pick which Docker/Kubernetes
endpoint a stack or container lives on, or audit endpoint health. Skip
bare Docker talk without Portainer. Load `portainer-safety` on every
Portainer turn. Stack deploy/delete → `portainer-stacks`; container stop/
remove → `portainer-containers`.

## Prefer live surface

No Portainer MCP was discovered in the live harness catalog. Prefer:

1. Portainer **API** with a base URL from operator config / env / MCP
   (if one appears later — discover tools from the live map; do not invent
   names)
2. Authenticated Portainer **UI** when API access is unavailable

Never hardcode a host. Never invent endpoint ids or names — list/resolve
this turn, or use exact names the user pasted.

## Craft

| Need | Approach |
| --- | --- |
| List endpoints | API environments list, or UI Environments |
| One endpoint | Resolve by id/name from the list; report type (Docker / Swarm / K8s) + status |
| Scope a stack/container ask | Resolve endpoint first, then load stacks/containers rules |
| Endpoint credentials / TLS | Out of scope to change without `portainer-safety` verb |

## Discover first

1. Resolve **base URL** from config/env — refuse guessing.
2. List endpoints before naming one in a mutate or stack deploy.
3. Report **name + id + type + status** — never paste API tokens or JWT.

## Procedure (read paths)

1. **Scope** — fleet list vs one named endpoint. **Done when** the ask is
   clear.
2. **List / resolve** — evidence from API/UI this turn. **Done when** every
   endpoint id you will cite was listed or user-pasted.
3. **Report** — short table (see shape). **Done when** no secrets appear.

## Report shape

- **name** / **id**
- **type** — Docker standalone, Swarm, Kubernetes (as Portainer reports)
- **status** — up / down / snapshot age when available
- **base URL** — product URL only; no credentials

## Out of scope

- Deploying or deleting stacks → `portainer-stacks` + `portainer-safety`
- Stopping or removing containers → `portainer-containers` +
  `portainer-safety`
- Changing endpoint access control, API keys, or TLS trust store without
  an explicit safety-gated verb
- Checked-in Compose file authorship (layout/merge) — Portainer UI/API
  ops against live endpoints only

## Related (this plugin)

- `portainer-stacks` — stack inventory and gated deploy
- `portainer-containers` — container inventory and gated ops
- `portainer-safety` — mutate / prune / credential refuse
